"🐢 woah, too slow...

🐚 git.repo.test --what unit --mode apply --resnap --timeout 1
   ├─ bound: 1s (--timeout)
   │  └─ let your shell call run past 31s, or its own clock ends this run first
   ├─ status
   │  └─ ⏱️ too slow (Xs)
   ├─ log
   │  ├─ stdout: .log/role=mechanic/skill=git.repo.test/what=unit/ISOTIME.stdout.log
   │  └─ stderr: .log/role=mechanic/skill=git.repo.test/what=unit/ISOTIME.stderr.log
   └─ ✋ ConstraintError: woah, too slow — past the 1s bound (--timeout)
      ├─ this speed defect is yours to root cause
      ├─ fix why it is slow: shared setup, real waits, redundant calls
      └─ a cut skips jest teardown: a server the suite detached may still run

🥥 did you know?
   ├─ find the slow suite: Read the log; a cut log lists only the files that finished, so the slow one never reported
   ├─ or bisect it: rerun with --scope over half the files, then half again
   ├─ snapshots may be partly written: rerun --resnap once the suite is fast
   └─ no call may run past 420s: make the suite fast, never the bound wide
"
`;

