exports[`git.repo.test.sh bound given: [case16] a fuse that cannot take hold of or mark the run, through the skill when: [t0] the watchdog run does not get its own process group then: stderr matches snapshot 1`] = `
"🐢 bummer dude...

🐚 git.repo.test --what lint
   ├─ bound: 420s (default)
   │  └─ let your shell call run past 450s, or its own clock ends this run first
   ├─ status
   │  └─ 💥 malfunction (Xs)
   └─ log: .log/role=mechanic/skill=git.repo.test/what=lint/ISOTIME.stderr.log

💥 MalfunctionError: the bound could not take hold of the run
   ├─ why: the run got process group 1, not its own (PID); a cut would miss its children
   └─ note: the run's leader (PID) is stopped; any child it had already started may still run, in group 1

🥥 did you know?
   ├─ install gnu coreutils, and the bound uses gtimeout instead of this watchdog
   └─ find leftovers with: ps -o pid,pgid,args -g 1
"
`;

